  "reviewNote": "Completed two full English/Czech readings of the final sixteen rows after repairing the draft and refining fluency. Verified Shane’s low-heart hostility and relapse, exhausted walk, hangover, chicken enthusiasm, all seasonal food-and-drink jokes, tropical plants, the Luau stomach metaphor, Marnie’s fair animals, aging discomfort and winter inertia. Applied Slavnost vajec, Květinový tanec, Luau and Jarmark údolí Stardew; checked every marker. No further issue found.",
  "rows": [
    {
      "target": "Characters/Dialogue/MarriageDialogueShane",
      "key": "Bad_6",
      "field": null,
      "source": "What do you want? You sound like Marnie on one of her bad days. Go away.$a",
      "translation": "Co chceš? Mluvíš jako Marnie, když má zrovna špatný den. Jdi pryč.$a",
